 "notes": "Spreadsheet printout (PDF), no printed places, no team scores, no date; date 2010-05-04 taken from file name (morsegirlsresults_may4). Header: 'KVAC League Meet #3 @ Morse, GIRLS (EL, Morse, Oak Hill, Gardiner, Mt. View)'. Codes EL/ELHS, MV/MTV/Mount View, MOR/Morse, GAR/GARD/GARDNER/Gardener, OH/Oak Hill expanded to Edward Little, Mount View, Morse, Gardiner, Oak Hill; the file never spells out EL (Edward Little is the only EL school among these teams, from outside knowledge). PLACES: the sheet prints none, so place is null on every row; rows are in file order. TIMES: kept exactly as printed, including the trailing hundredths digit (13.34, 5:46.24), which are hand times converted to FAT (+0.24). Printed '1:06.4' (M. DD) and '1:22.4' (A. LeClerc) have no such digit and are kept. Typos: '11.29.28' (K. Porter) written 11:29.28; '13.50.24' (L.Hayward) 13:50.24; '36.84-' (L Stauffer) 36.84. EVENT LABELS: '4x8 Relay' = 4x800 Meter Relay, '4x4 Relay' = 4x400 Meter Relay, '1600m RW' = 1600 Meter Race Walk (times unsorted), 'Polevault' = Pole Vault, 'Shotput' = Shot Put, 'Highjump' = High Jump. Triple Jump printed 22-1.5 for K. Clutier and 31-11 for E. Hillman (unusual but kept). Long Jump: one list of 24 rows plus two more (13-4 A. Chisholm EL, 12-3.5 A. Lever EL) printed in the next column on the next print page; the 6-1.5 to 9-9.5 rows (Boaden, Kimble, Cox, McDonough, Laflamme, Iman, Howell) sit directly under the list with no header so are kept as long jump but could be a separate event. FIELD MARK FIXES: '65.8.5' (Basinger javelin) -> 65-8.5; '52.10' (Caron discus) -> 52-10; '57' (Basiger discus) -> 57-00; '28' (Morency shot) -> 28-00. NAMES kept as printed incl. misspellings (Beauparlant/Beauparlaunt, Hilman/Hillman, Hartnet/Hartnett, 'M. DD', 'Saveign', 'Buckalon', 'Belltlean'); school 'Gardener'/'Garedener' read as Gardiner; relay school 'Mt Veiw' read as Mount View. Relay rows have no athlete names; ELHS A/B kept as 'Edward Little A/B'. Two 400m schools ('E. Bell-Huerth MO', 'E. Buczkowski M') are cut off in the print but read as MOR from the text layer."
